<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-AU">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Privacy Policy | Intelligent Talent Matching Platform</title>
    <meta name="description" content="TalentMatch helps candidates find jobs and employers find candidates using intelligent profile and job matching." />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/lib/css/font-awesome.min.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/lib/css/modern-normalize.min.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/global.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/policy.css" />
    <script src="/lib/js/jquery.min.js"></script>
</head>
<body class="<%= theme === 'DARK' ? 'dark-mode' : '' %>">
<%- include('../partials/public-header/public-header'); %>
<main class="policy-page">
    <section class="policy-page__hero" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
        <div class="policy-page__hero-inner">
            <p class="policy-page__eyebrow">
                Legal
            </p>
            <h1 id="privacy-title" class="policy-page__title">
                Privacy Policy
            </h1>
            <p class="policy-page__intro">
                This Privacy Policy explains how TalentMatch collects, uses,
                stores, and protects personal information when candidates,
                employers, and visitors use the Intelligent Talent Matching Platform.
            </p>
            <p class="policy-page__updated">
                Last updated: 31 May 2026
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="policy-page__layout" aria-label="Privacy policy content">
        <aside class="policy-page__sidebar" aria-label="Privacy policy sections">
            <nav class="policy-page__nav">
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#overview">Overview</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#information-we-collect">Information we collect</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#how-we-use-information">How we use information</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#matching-and-recommendations">Matching and recommendations</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#sharing-information">Sharing information</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#storage-and-security">Storage and security</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#cookies-and-sessions">Cookies and sessions</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#your-rights">Your rights</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#contact">Contact</a>
            </nav>
        </aside>
        <article class="policy-page__content">
            <section id="overview" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title">1. Overview</h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    TalentMatch is a recruitment platform designed to help candidates
                    find suitable job opportunities and help employers identify suitable
                    candidates. To provide these services, the platform processes
                    account, profile, job, application, search, and recommendation data.
                </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    We aim to collect only the information needed to operate the
                    platform, improve matching accuracy, support account security,
                    and provide a functional recruitment experience.
                </p>
            </section>
            <section id="information-we-collect" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title">2. Information we collect</h2>
                <h3 class="policy-page__subheading">Account information</h3>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    When you create an account, we may collect information such as
                    your name, email address, phone number, password hash, account
                    role, account status, theme preference, membership status, and
                    profile avatar reference.
                </p>
                <h3 class="policy-page__subheading">Candidate profile information</h3>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    Candidate profiles may include education, major or field of study,
                    years of experience, work experience, skills, preferred working
                    mode, preferred location, preferred job type, availability,
                    resume links, portfolio links, LinkedIn links, and profile summaries.
                </p>
                <h3 class="policy-page__subheading">Employer and company information</h3>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    Employer profiles may include company name, company description,
                    industry, company location, company contact details, company
                    website, company size, company values, and company avatar reference.
                </p>
                <h3 class="policy-page__subheading">Job and application information</h3>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    Job postings may include job title, company information, job
                    description, required education, required experience, required
                    skills, work mode, location, salary range, job type, closing date,
                    and application records.
                </p>
                <h3 class="policy-page__subheading">Usage and technical information</h3>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    We may collect technical information required to operate the
                    service, including session identifiers, authentication status,
                    last activity time, browser interactions, and basic request data.
                </p>
            </section>
            <section id="how-we-use-information" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title">3. How we use information</h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    We use personal information to provide and improve the platform,
                    including to:
                </p>
                <ul class="policy-page__list">
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Create and manage user accounts.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Support candidate and employer profiles.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Display job postings and candidate profiles.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Enable searching, filtering, saved jobs, and applications.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Generate job and candidate recommendations.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Provide notifications and account updates.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Apply membership-based recommendation limits.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Maintain platform security and prevent misuse.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Improve the usability and reliability of the service.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>
            <section id="matching-and-recommendations" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title">4. Matching and recommendations</h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    TalentMatch uses structured profile and job information to compare
                    candidates with job postings and employers with candidate profiles.
                    Matching may consider factors such as skills, education, experience,
                    location, work mode, job type, profile summaries, and job descriptions.
                </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    Recommendation scores are intended to assist users in finding
                    relevant opportunities or candidates. They should not be treated
                    as a final employment decision. Employers and candidates remain
                    responsible for reviewing suitability independently.
                </p>
            </section>
            <section id="sharing-information" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title">5. Sharing information</h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    Candidate profile information may be visible to employers where
                    required for candidate discovery, matching, and applications.
                    Employer and job posting information may be visible to candidates
                    for job discovery and matching.
                </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    We do not sell personal information. Information may be shared
                    only where needed to operate the platform, comply with legal
                    obligations, enforce platform terms, protect security, or support
                    user-requested functionality.
                </p>
            </section>
            <section id="storage-and-security" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title">6. Storage and security</h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    TalentMatch uses technical and organisational controls to protect
                    information against unauthorised access, misuse, loss, and
                    modification. Passwords are stored as password hashes rather than
                    plain text.
                </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    No system can be guaranteed to be completely secure. Users should
                    use strong passwords, keep account details private, and contact us
                    if they suspect unauthorised access to their account.
                </p>
            </section>
            <section id="cookies-and-sessions" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title">7. Cookies and sessions</h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    TalentMatch uses session cookies to keep users signed in, remember
                    basic preferences such as theme selection, and protect account
                    workflows. These cookies are used for platform functionality and
                    are not intended for third-party advertising.
                </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    You may disable cookies in your browser settings, but some platform
                    features may not work correctly without them.
                </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    For more information about the cookies used by TalentMatch,
                    including their purpose, duration, and how they are managed,
                    please refer to our
                    <a class="policy-page__inline-link" href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
                </p>
            </section>
            <section id="your-rights" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title">8. Your rights and choices</h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    Users may update account, candidate, and employer profile information
                    through their account settings where available. Users may also request
                    assistance with accessing, correcting, or deleting personal information.
                </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    Some information may need to be retained for security, legal,
                    operational, or recordkeeping purposes.
                </p>
            </section>
            <section id="contact" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title">9. Contact</h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    For privacy questions, account support, or requests about your
                    personal information, contact the TalentMatch support team.
                </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    Email:
                    <a class="policy-page__inline-link" href="mailto:support@talentmatch.com">
                        support@talentmatch.com
                    </a>
                </p>
            </section>
            <section class="policy-page__note" aria-label="Important note">
                <h2 class="policy-page__note-title">
                    Academic Project Disclaimer
                </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    TalentMatch and all associated policies, terms, and documentation have been
                    developed as part of CSIT314 – Software Development Methodologies at the
                    University of Wollongong for academic assessment purposes. These documents
                    have not been reviewed by legal professionals and are not intended to
                    constitute legal advice or create legally binding obligations. Any future
                    production or commercial deployment should be subject to independent legal,
                    privacy, and regulatory review.
                </p>
            </section>
        </article>
    </section>
</main>
<%- include('../partials/footer/footer'); %>
<script src="/js/global.js"></script>
</body>
</html>